<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 6-mth T-bills 98 pct sold, yield 169 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 6-mth T-bills 98 pct sold, yield 169 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 7.5 billion levs of six-month floater coupon T-bills was 98.33 percent sold, yielding 168.62 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance for Monday's auction by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15 percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		    BG 3020296029</p>
<p> Auction date		    November 11, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			November 13, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		   May 14, 1997 Bids received</p>
<p>							7,500 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	     70.42 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		   7,375 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	    70.64 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity   168.62 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
